@ The File menu offers the dialog, a submenu with a text field in which a
path can be typed or pasted (useful when no desktop dialog is available),
reloading the current file, and quitting. The text field returns true when
Enter is pressed, which counts as pressing Load. Reloading reads the file
again from disk, which is handy while editing a \texttt{.usda} file in another
window.

<<The File menu>>=
if (ImGui::BeginMenu("File"))
{
    if (ImGui::MenuItem("Open...", "Ctrl+O"))
        openFileDialog();
    if (ImGui::BeginMenu("Open path"))
    {
        ImGui::SetNextItemWidth(420.0f);
